-- title:
--   Affine quotient by a finite locally free equivalence relation
-- statement:
--   Let $A$, $B$, $C$ be commutative rings in a common universe, with $A$ a $C$-algebra, and let $s, t \colon A \to B$ be two ring homomorphisms. Assume that $B$ is a finite projective $A$-module for the $A$-algebra structure given by $s$, and likewise for the one given by $t$; that the subring generated by the images of $s$ and $t$ is all of $B$, i.e. $\operatorname{range} s \sqcup \operatorname{range} t = \top$; that for every commutative ring $T$ the relation on ring homomorphisms $A \to T$ defined by $x \sim y$ if and only if there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon B \to T$ with $\varphi \circ s = x$ and $\varphi \circ t = y$ is an equivalence relation; that the structure map $C \to A$ is injective; and that for $a \in A$ one has $s(a) = t(a)$ precisely when $a$ lies in the image of $C \to A$, so that $C$ is identified with the ring of invariants $\{a \in A : s(a) = t(a)\}$. The conclusion is that $A$ is a finite, projective and faithfully flat $C$-module, and that the square of commutative rings with the two copies of $C \to A$ out of $C$ and with $s$ and $t$ into $B$ is a pushout; equivalently, the map $A \otimes_C A \to B$, $a \otimes a' \mapsto s(a)t(a')$, is an isomorphism.
--
--   This is the affine case of the theorem on quotients of schemes by finite locally free equivalence relations: $\operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} C$ is finite locally free and faithfully flat, and $\operatorname{Spec} B \rightrightarrows \operatorname{Spec} A$ is its kernel pair, so that $\operatorname{Spec} C$ is the quotient. It is used to produce an affine quotient in [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_affine_quotient_of_finiteLocallyFree_equivalenceRelation`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_affine_quotient_of_finiteLocallyFree_equivalenceRelation).
